  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>An amine on reaction with benzenesulphonyl chloride produces a compound insoluble in alkaline solution. This amine can be prepared by ammonolysis of ethyl chloride.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a2d89ebc-0f1a-4494-8fec-b588ff427386-image.png\" style=\"width: 263px; height: 174px;\" /></p><p>It has to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> amine because on reaction with benzene sulphonylchloride it gives water in soluble product. As it is formed by ammonolysis of ethylchloride, so it has to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>NH</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Et</mi></math> type.</p>",
